[1.021399, "o", "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[1.021609, "o", "\r\n  The causal model — YAML spec + Mermaid graph\r\n"]
[1.025024, "o", "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[1.02531, "o", "\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2moutputs/demo/final_model_spec.yaml  |  outputs/demo/causal_graph.mmd\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[1.025401, "o", "\u001b[1mMermaid causal graph (renders in any Mermaid viewer):\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[1.027765, "o", "    graph LR\r\n        Workload -->|\"positive, conf:0.48\"| Stress\r\n        Teamsupport -->|\"negative, conf:0.47\"| Anxiety\r\n        Projectstructure -->|\"positive, conf:0.46\"| Self-confidenceatwork\r\n        Managerguidance -->|\"positive, conf:0.46\"| Stress\r\n        Managertrust -->|\"positive, conf:0.46\"| Self-confidenceatwork\r\n        Micromanagement -->|\"positive, conf:0.45\"| Anxiety\r\n        Schedulecontrol -->|\"negative, conf:0.45\"| Stress\r\n        Communicationclarity -->|\"positive, conf:0.44\"| Uncertaintyaboutpriorities\r\n        Meetingload -->|\"positive, conf:0.44\"| Stress\r\n        Organizationalculture -->|\"positive, conf:0.34\"| Jobcrafting"]
[1.027936, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.027984, "o", "\u001b[1mYAML model spec — variables:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.031214, "o", "  variables:\r\n  - name: Anxiety\r\n    type: contextual\r\n    definition: Anxiety inferred from relationships across chunks.\r\n    aliases: []\r\n    chunk_frequency: 2\r\n    confidence: 0.67\r\n  - name: Self-confidence at work\r\n    type: contextual\r\n    definition: Self-confidence at work inferred from relationships across chunks.;\r\n      Self-confidence inferred from relationships across chunks.\r\n    aliases:\r\n    - Self-confidence\r\n    chunk_frequency: 2\r\n    confidence: 0.67\r\n  - name: Stress\r\n"]
[1.031683, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m"]
[1.035216, "o", "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[1.03545, "o", "\r\n  Quote-level provenance — verify before you trust\r\n"]
[1.038993, "o", "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[1.039227, "o", "\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.03924, "o", "\u001b[2moutputs/demo/evidence_report.md  |  outputs/demo/methods_draft.md\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[1.039276, "o", "\u001b[1mEvery hypothesis carries its source quote:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[1.042714, "o", "  ### H1: Workload has a positive effect on Stress.\r\n  - Data confidence: **0.34**\r\n  - Literature consensus: **weak** (score 0.00)\r\n  - Novelty flag: **False**\r\n  - Supporting quote: _I feel overwhelmed when I have too many deadlines at work._\r\n  \r\n  ### H2: Team support has a negative effect on Anxiety.\r\n  - Data confidence: **0.34**\r\n  - Literature consensus: **weak** (score 0.00)\r\n  - Novelty flag: **False**\r\n  - Supporting quote: _Team support really helps when I'm stressed about deadlines._\r\n  \r\n"]
[1.04274, "o", "  ### H3: Project structure has a positive effect on Self-confidence at work.\r\n  - Data confidence: **0.33**\r\n  - Literature consensus: **weak** (score 0.00)\r\n  - Novelty flag: **False**\r\n  - Supporting quote: _When I have a clear project timeline and regular check-ins with my supervisor, I feel much more confident and productive._\r\n  \r\n"]
[1.043221, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1mAnd every extracted relationship links back to a chunk + verbatim quote:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[1.046173, "o", "  # Structured model draft (machine-assisted)\r\n  \r\n  ## Structural coverage (heuristic)\r\n  - Score: **0.50** (see project docs for what this does and does not mean.)\r\n  - Testability (heuristic): **0.60**\r\n  \r\n  ## Extracted content\r\n  \r\n  ### Chunk `respondent_1_chunk_0`\r\n  - **Relationship** (direct): Workload → Stress — _More deadlines increase overwhelm._ (confidence 0.9) [evidence 1]\r\n  - **Relationship** (direct): Manager guidance → Stress — _Unclear guidance worsens stress._ (confidence 0.85) [evidence 2]\r\n  - **Relationship** (direct): Communication clarity → Uncertainty about priorities — _Lack of communication creates uncertainty._ (confidence 0.8) [evidence 3]\r\n"]
[1.046521, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m"]
[1.049815, "o", "───────────────────────────────────────────"]
[1.050135, "o", "\r\n  What the model still doesn't know\r\n"]
[1.053972, "o", "───────────────────────────────────────────"]
[1.05426, "o", "\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2moutputs/demo/gap_report.json  |  outputs/demo/clarification_plan.json\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[1.114683, "o", "  structural coverage : 0.50   (heuristic)\r\n  model testability   : 0.60   (heuristic)\r\n\r\n  gaps found          : 10\r\n    - [medium] Relationship references variables that are not defined in extracted variable lists: anxiety, micromanagement\r\n    - [medium] Relationship references variables that are not defined in extracted variable lists: anxiety, team support\r\n    - [medium] Relationship references variables that are not defined in extracted variable lists: communication clarity, uncertainty about priorities\r\n    - [medium] Relationship references variables that are not defined in extracted variable lists: job crafting, organizational culture\r\n\r\n  clarification questions : 10\r\n    - Q1: Which exact constructs define these referenced variables and how should they be measured?\r\n    - Q10: Which exact constructs define these referenced variables and how should they be measured?\r\n    - Q2: Which exact constructs define these referenced variables and how should they be measured?\r\n    - Q3: Which exact constructs"]
[1.114771, "o", " define these referenced variables and how should they be measured?\r\n\r\n  → asking a follow-up researcher question next is recommended before these gaps can be closed.\r\n"]
